    <string name="help_add_manual">Open Quick Settings, tap the pencil (edit) and drag the “Graphics: …” tiles to the active area.</string>
    <string name="help_message">QUICK SETTINGS TILES\n\n• Graphics: Balanced — lowers the games’ resolution to %1$d%%. A good middle ground between quality and performance.\n\n• Graphics: Performance — lowers it to %2$d%%. More FPS, blurrier image.\n\nTo change these values, use the ⋮ menu > Adjust intensity.\n\nOnly one profile is active at a time. Tapping the active tile turns the profile off. You may need to reopen the game for the change to take effect.\n\nRebooting the device undoes the profile. With “Keep until reboot” (in Adjust) on, the system is also prevented from overwriting the values during that period. “Restore” undoes it right away and also cleans leftover entries (for example, from games you uninstalled).\n\nFor the reduction to take effect, the app puts the games in the system’s Performance mode and, when the profile is turned off, returns them to Standard mode.\n\nUnchecked items in the list are never changed. If Shizuku is not yet authorized, the tile itself asks for permission.\n\nHOW TO ADD\n%3$s</string>
